  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the aggressive protest scene as embodying selective religious intolerance",
  "description": "The user is implicitly projected onto the scene and the central figure, as the meme uses the visual of the angry man and the text to create a caricature of religious hypocrisy. The user is invited to see themselves as the embodiment of the behavior described — showing intolerance toward others while expecting tolerance for their own — thus projecting their own potential or perceived behavior onto the scene. The deictic projection is implicit, not explicit, but the framing of the meme (the angry man pointing forward, the text labeling the behavior) creates a direct address to the viewer, making them the subject of the critique.",
